# Kling Element + bound voice (O3 Pro)

## Rule

Dialogue beats with an **active Element + create-voice** must submit with:

1. **`@Image1` = registered Element pose** (frontal or emotion-matched refer) — not a random library PNG
2. **Locked voice line** in prompt (`Tessa speaks in a warm gentle conversational pace…`) — not generic `<<<voice_N>>>` or ad-hoc “speaks warmly”
3. **`element_list`** on WaveSpeed O3 Pro submit (Jessica/Miranda/etc.)

Mismatch → generic Kling TTS even when logs show correct `element_id`.

## Char ref gate (locked library drops)

| Action | Heal behavior |
|---|---|
| User drops library tile on Char ref | **Validate only** — `sync_element_char_ref_status(..., heal_mismatch=False)` |
| O3 Generate / submit | **Validate only** — same; mismatch → `ELEMENT_VISUAL_MISMATCH` toast |
| Sidecar migrate / session-state load | **Do not redirect** locked library refs when the tile file still exists — validate gate only |

**NEVER** redirect a user-locked `library/images/sources/` path to an Element pose when that library file still exists on disk. **NEVER** `shutil.copy2` (or any write) into `Event_*/library/images/sources/` from heal/sync/align code.

Regression: `Production/tools/tests/test_library_sources_immutable.py`, `test_beat_ref_drop_lock.py`.

## Enforcement

| Layer | Location |
|---|---|
| Submit handler | `handle_bg_submit_arlo_o3_voice` — align + `ELEMENT_VISUAL_MISMATCH` gate |
| Element pipeline | `kling_o3_element_beat_pipeline.run_pipeline` |
| Sidecar migrate | `align_beat_reference_to_element` (skip **still_insert** beats) |
| Registry paths | `kling_character_registry.set_prod_root()` via `init_bg_paths` |

## Still inserts

Do **not** auto-align `reference_image` on `still_insert` beats — they use library still in option 1 + ElevenLabs TTS, not Element O3.

## Lorelai Element

**Kling display name:** `Laurel` (Kling cannot pronounce "Lorelai"). Registry key, sidecar `speaker`, and pose paths stay `Lorelai`. All Kling surfaces — `element_list.element_name`, O3 voice lines (`Laurel speaks in a …`), and `@Image1 (Laurel)` — use **Laurel** via `kling_element_display_name()`.

Poses: `Lorelai/poses/lorelai_canonical_neutral.png`, `lorelai_explaining.png`, `lorelai_shocked.png`

Re-register after pose swap: `python3 scripts/setup_all_kling_character_voices.py --char Lorelai --force`

